## Why this is WIP and not a closure

The strong consolidation overstates by claiming derivation-target
items as established consequences. The narrow consolidation
(strictly the parabola-Born-binary-axis chain plus `q_2` by
definition plus sector-restricted `i² = −1`) is already in the
corpus and doesn't need a freestanding doc.

The right disposition for this stage is *staging note*:

1. The per-context audit is *useful* (organizational, navigational,
   discipline-bounding).
2. The strong consolidation is *not yet earned* (audit identifies
   the gaps).
3. The path forward is either (a) carry out the derivations the
   audit names as targets, or (b) absorb this doc into the broader
   QM-reframing doc where its function is *demonstrating
   substrate-native consolidation as a method*, not claiming a
   substantive new result.

Either path takes this WIP doc further. As a standalone result,
it sits at the level of "useful audit, no new structural content."

